22:["$","div",null,{"className":"px-6 pb-5","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed","children":"No, Ace & Tate does not offer NHS-funded eye tests. All eye tests at Ace & Tate are private, starting from £25 for a standard examination and from £50 for a comprehensive test. They do not participate in the NHS optical voucher scheme for glasses either. If you are looking for a free NHS eye test, you would need to visit an optician that participates in the NHS scheme, such as Boots Opticians or Specsavers. You can use eyetest.co.uk to compare NHS and private options near you."}]}]
23:["$","details","3",{"className":"group bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-6 py-5 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-navy)] text-left","children":"Are Ace & Tate frames good quality?"}],["$","svg",null,{"className":"w-5 h-5 text-gray-400 flex-shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","fill":"none","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","children":["$","path",null,{"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","d":"M19 9l-7 7-7-7"}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-6 pb-5","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed","children":"Ace & Tate frames are designed in-house at their Amsterdam studio and manufactured using high-quality materials including Italian Mazzucchelli acetate, lightweight stainless steel, and increasingly, recycled and bio-based acetate. The brand puts significant emphasis on design and build quality, with frames that feel solid and well-finished. Hinges, nose pads, and temple tips are designed for comfort and durability. As a certified B-Corp, Ace & Tate also meets verified standards for social and environmental performance, which extends to their material sourcing and production processes."}]}]]}]
24:["$","details","4",{"className":"group bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-6 py-5 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-navy)] text-left","children":"Can I book an Ace & Tate eye test online?"}],["$","svg",null,{"className":"w-5 h-5 text-gray-400 flex-shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","fill":"none","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","children":["$","path",null,{"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","d":"M19 9l-7 7-7-7"}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-6 pb-5","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed","children":"Yes, you can book an eye test at your nearest Ace & Tate store through eyetest.co.uk. Simply enter your postcode, find the nearest location, and select an available appointment slot. You can also book directly through the Ace & Tate website or by contacting the store. Booking through eyetest.co.uk lets you compare availability and prices across multiple opticians in your area, making it easy to find the best option for your needs and schedule."}]}]]}]
25:["$","details","5",{"className":"group bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-6 py-5 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-navy)] text-left","children":"What makes Ace & Tate different from other opticians?"}],["$","svg",null,{"className":"w-5 h-5 text-gray-400 flex-shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","fill":"none","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","children":["$","path",null,{"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","d":"M19 9l-7 7-7-7"}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"px-6 pb-5","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed","children":"Ace & Tate operates on a direct-to-consumer model that cuts out the traditional middlemen in the eyewear industry — the brand designs its own frames, works directly with manufacturers, and sells through its own stores and website. This means they can offer designer-quality glasses at a significantly lower price than traditional opticians selling third-party designer labels. Their transparent pricing — frames with lenses from £98 — their design-first approach, sustainability commitments, and curated retail experience set them apart from both high-street chains and luxury boutiques."}]}]]}]
